{"name":"Prom Queen","hex":"#9b1dcd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"prom queen","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["In colleges and high schools, a young woman chosen, or sometimes elected by her peers, to have an honored status over the school's prom and related activities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prom_queen"}],"entries":[{"title":"Prom Queen (Glee)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Prom Queen\" is the twentieth episode of the second season of the American musical television series Glee, and the forty-second overall. It aired May 10, 2011, on Fox in the United States. The episode was written by series creator Ian Brennan, directed by Eric Stoltz, and featured the return of guest star Jonathan Groff. In \"Prom Queen\", the McKinley High School glee club New Directions is tapped to provide the music for the school's junior prom. The episode shows the myriad dramas surrounding a high school prom, with the high-stakes race for prom king and queen that involves five members of the glee club, students scrambling to find dates and outfits, and the delights and disappointments of the prom itself."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prom_Queen_(Glee)"},{"title":"Prom Queen (Lil Wayne song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Prom Queen\" is the lead single from Lil Wayne's album, Rebirth. The track is produced by Infamous and Andrew \"Drew\" Correa. The song is written by and contains backing vocals from Shanell Woodgett. The song made its official debut on January 27, appearing on Lil Wayne's MySpace page. The following day, \"Prom Queen\" was made available for purchase on all online music stores and Lil Wayne performed the single live for the first time during a concert in San Diego, which was streamed live on AT&T's FREEdom of Choice and Mobile Music Facebook pages that evening. The song features the Auto-Tune effect."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f3/Lil_Wayne-Prom_Queen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prom_Queen_(Lil_Wayne_song)"},{"title":"Prom","blocks":[{"text":"A promenade dance or prom is a formal dance party for graduating high school students at the end of the school year."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Preprom.jpg/330px-Preprom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prom"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/MaxAdler.png/120px-MaxAdler.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d1/MaxAdler.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/MaxAdler.png/120px-MaxAdler.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMaxAdler.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Chris_Colfer_2011_Shankbone.JPG/500px-Chris_Colfer_2011_Shankbone.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Chris_Colfer_2011_Shankbone.JPG/1280px-Chris_Colfer_2011_Shankbone.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Chris_Colfer_2011_Shankbone.JPG/500px-Chris_Colfer_2011_Shankbone.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChris_Colfer_2011_Shankbone.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Wrist_corsages.jpg/500px-Wrist_corsages.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/W